Scenario 15: Frontend On Worker-1, Backend Scaled To Worker-3 (Cilium)
Interviewer

A new backend pod comes up on Worker-3. How does frontend reach it?

Model Answer

"Frontend never talks directly to pod IPs.

It uses the Kubernetes Service.

Plain Text
Frontend
↓
Service VIP
↓
Cilium eBPF LB
↓
Backend Pod Worker-2
or
Backend Pod Worker-3

When HPA adds new backend pods, Cilium updates the eBPF service maps automatically.

New pods start receiving traffic without application changes."

One-line senior interview closing answer

When asked any autoscaling scenario, finish with:

"I always look at the complete chain: Metrics → HPA → Scheduler → Cluster Autoscaler → CNI (Cilium) → Application behavior. The issue is usually somewhere in that path."

That answer immediately signals senior-level troubleshooting thinking
